on honestly so  we've got to win a lot we've spoken a  lot about the vote um  tomorrow uh to be fair and mr reynolds i  am quite keen to talk about some other  issues um  as well and the government's decided to  tighten up border restrictions  in light of these new variants now we've  all seen the images of  instagram influencers going on holiday  posting beach  or poolside snaps if you go on holiday  right now you being selfish  sorry i missed that last bit uh sophie  but i think you were talking about  the restrictions on airports and  travelers coming into the country  i just don't understand why it's taking  so long to put those arrangements in  place we've seen what went on  in other countries and i think we were  told initially that those just weren't  effective they weren't worth doing  but clearly they are so i don't  understand why it's taken so long i  think there is a significant degree of  national concern  about why we've been so slow to make  sure our borders are secure and we're  stopping new strains coming into the  country  is there some personal responsibility to  hear though as well  are you being selfish if you go on  holiday now  well it obviously depends the  circumstances about which you are  traveling but yes i mean let's be clear  though people have  in the main throughout this pandemic  abided by some really tough  restrictions yes we all know some high  profile infringements that have taken  place but people have  not seen family members they've been  students away from home who haven't been  able to go home  and see their family so let's not try  and let the government  get away with blaming the public or  blaming people for their personal  conduct for  where the pandemic response has gone  wrong i think that lets them off the  hook  the majority of british people have  abided by really tough restrictions  and they've done it in the national  interest and they've done it whatever  the personal cost to them  has been and we have to recognize that  one thing that it does seem people  perhaps not always obeying the rules are  on is the  quarantine or on self-isolating some of  the surveys showing pretty low number of  people  who have been in south isolating for the  full amount of time given that  do you think people should be put in  hotels quarantine hotels like they do in  other countries  if they return to the uk from abroad  if that is the most effective way uh to  tackle that i i'd look at that i'm not  sure necessarily it is  the case i mean i think most people do  abide by the restrictions  have been able to stay at home if  there's a specific court i've seen  things that look like they may have  worked  quite successfully in other countries so  there's best practice there but again  the problem is sophie we're behind the  curve on this we haven't  acted quickly enough we haven't done  what other countries have done so  there's plenty of things  that we can learn from but as i say i  think most people have abided by some  tough restrictions whatever the personal  cost to them

